{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Lest I consume you, etc.</b> For one who provokes his master to his face is not comparable to one who does so not in his presence. And His saying <b>on the way</b> — here He alluded that He does not say this for all times, but only for the time when they are on the way; but in a city — עָז לָנוּ יַעֲלֶה בְּקִרְבֵּנוּ (Isaiah 26:1)." "<b>Or</b> it may intend according to the saying of the men of truth, that the wilderness was the dwelling place of Samael the wicked, and therefore he would many times prevail and kill some of them, because of the occasion that befell them through sin. And see the words of the Zohar (vol. II 156a) in explanation of the verse ״הַמִּדְבָּר הַגָּדוֹל וְהַנּוֹרָא״ (Deuteronomy 1:19). And therefore He said <b>lest I consume you on the way</b> — meaning, through the intermediary that is encountered on the way. Understand:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:20.446824897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}